{
  "record_id": "021",
  "problem": "Werner–Holevo zero-capacity boundary",
  "collection": "Original research investigation",
  "summary": "The environment-support restriction can force phi=|psi><psi|, so the assumed nontrivial comparison domain does not exist.",
  "review_status": "source_reviewed",
  "review_note": "No open interpretation blocker was recorded in the preceding source review. This is not a new independent mathematical verification.",
  "original": {
    "excerpt": "- D1 (derivation check, exact): verify the pure-output spectra claims symbolically; verify\n  the epsilon-expansion bookkeeping NUMERICALLY at high precision: for random (psi, phi)\n  kernel-avoiding pairs at x = 9/20, fit Ic((1-eps)psi + eps phi) against\n  c1*eps + O(eps^2 log eps) and confirm the fitted c1 matches\n  `-Tr[Λ(phi-psi) log Λ(psi)] + Tr[Λ^c(phi-psi) log Λ^c(psi)]` to >= 8 digits; also confirm\n  kernel-HITTING phi produce the -eps log(1/eps) plunge. GATE G0.\n\n[...]\n\n  over pure psi and kernel-avoiding states phi (parameterize phi on the 3-dim support\n  constraint; >= 150 restarts). A_1 > 0 anywhere",
    "context": "The proposed first-order test requires a distinct comparison state phi satisfying supp Lambda_x^c(phi) subset supp Lambda_x^c(psi). It treats this as a three-dimensional domain from which random kernel-avoiding pairs can be drawn.",
    "locator": "Research commission write, 2026-07-29T17:13:33.094Z, JSONL line 1522"
  },
  "witness": {
    "explanation": "The environment-support restriction can force phi=|psi><psi|, so the assumed nontrivial comparison domain does not exist.",
    "evidence": "For psi=|0> and 0<x<1, use Kraus operators K0=sqrt(1-x)I and K_(mu+1)=sqrt(x/2)A_mu, (A_mu)_(jk)=epsilon_(mu j k). The complementary output has kernel vector z=(0,1,0,0). Positivity and support inclusion imply Tr(K1 phi K1^dagger)=0, hence supp(phi) subset ker K1=span{|0>}. Since phi has trace one it equals |0><0|. The claimed random distinct-pair construction therefore fails already in this exact instance; generic tests in the recorded check also had one-dimensional allowed support.",
    "scope": "argument_invalid"
  },
